 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the city of New York to lease certain parkland in the borough of the Bronx to the New York Botanical Garden for a term of 99 years",
    "basePrintNo": "S3992",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3992-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "New York City",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3992\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto authorize the city of New York to lease certain parkland in the\nborough of the Bronx to the New York Botanical Garden for a term of 99\nyears\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThe purpose of this bill is authorize\nthe City of New York to lease certain parklands along the Dr.\nTheodore Kazimiroff Boulevard to the New York Botanical Garden so\nthat such parklands may be enhanced for better enjoyment by the\ngeneral public.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection 1: Authorizes the City of New York to lease approximately 3.84\nacres of parkland to the New York Botanical Gardens so that the\nBotanical Gardens may enhance this parkland area and utilize it more\neffectively as one of the Garden's public gateway entrances. Such\nlease shall be for 99 years and commence within three years of this\nbill becoming law.\n\nSection 2: Such property transfer shall not be subject to New York\nCity Charter sections 197-c and 197-d (Uniform Land Use Review\nProcedure and Council Review of City Planning Commission Actions).\n\nSection 3: Provides that the current uses of the parkland shall remain\nand continue to be used as parklands under the terms of the lease\nagreement.\n\nSection 4: This provision provides a description of the property to be\ntransferred under the terms of the 99 year lease. Such property is\napproximately 3.84 acres and is bounded by the Dr. Theodore\nKazimiroff Boulevard, Metro-North Railroad, Bedford Park Boulevard,\nand the Mosholu Parkway. The parcel is approximately 995 feet\nlong(north to south) and 235 feet wide (east to west). This property,\nat one time, was part of the New York Botanical Garden property, but\nwas transferred to the City of New York in 1937 for a proposed road\nconstruction project that never occurred. This bill reverses that\ntransaction so that the New York Botanical Garden can expand its area\nfor receiving visitors and exhibiting horticultural specimens.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis bill authorizes the City of New York and the New\nYork Botanical Garden to enter into a 99 year lease for the property\ndescribed above. Giving additional control to the Botanical Gardens\nover this 3.84 acre parcel will enable the Gardens to enhance their\nentrance to the Gardens from the Metro-North station that adjoins\nthe park. Thereby, enhancing the visual and environmental experience\nof visitors to the Gardens.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n\n",
